  "worked_solution": "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t))=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t))=1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t))^{2}+(1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}\u2061(t)+{sin}^{2}\u2061(t)+2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)+1+{cos}^{2}\u2061(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)+1+{cos}^{2}\u2061(t)-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{2+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t)+{cos}^{2}\u2061(t)}\\,\\text{d}t\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
